string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n        section: Required topic: overview/reasoning/tool_use/multi_agent/outlook\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nRead the PDF and update report.json.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"paper\", \"editable\": [\"report.json\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"report.json\"], \"verify_commands\": [], \"required_pages\": [1, 2, 3], \"note_topics\": [\"overview\", \"reasoning\", \"tool_use\", \"multi_agent\", \"outlook\"], \"max_model_calls\": 3}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nPaper workflow:\n1. Plan, baseline pytest, read report.json and paper.json; call read_pdf ONCE for the task's full page range.\nThis extracts to local storage and logs read_pdf.py; only bounded batches reach the model. Do not print all pages.\n2. Read the delivered page batches in order. Record a topic's supported findings as soon as useful; do not\nwait until both questions are answered. The next batch follows successful actions automatically. On an\naction error, correct it using the retained batch. Do not call read_pdf/task_status just to advance.\nUse only evidence ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n3. Update the same topic note incrementally, preserving earlier confirmed facts and citations. Each final\ntopic note must contain its two answers, PDF page numbers and continuous exact quotations supporting ALL\nanswer items, within 1500 characters.\nUse write_note(title=..., content=..., evidence_ids=['ev-...'], section='overview') with the actual topic.\n4. After full coverage, reuse all five final notes, build report.json across actions if needed, test, finish plan.\nThis agent already has versioned evidence, bounded page selection, note reuse, tools and verification.\nMulti-agent collaboration and training are future suggestions, not implemented features.\n\nCourse progress (new evidence below can satisfy pending items):\n{\"phase\": \"read\", \"next_requirement\": \"PDF pages not yet sent: 1,2,3\", \"remaining_count\": 7, \"requests_left\": 2, \"baseline_done\": 0, \"changed_files\": [], \"verified_current\": 0, \"required_checks\": 0, \"last_response_classification\": \"empty\", \"unseen_evidence_count\": 4, \"queued_recall_count\": 4}\nPrevious action excerpt (reference only):\n\nLatest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\n\nRecent project tool results:\n[{\"tool\": \"read_file\", \"result\": {\"path\": \"report.json\", \"file_hash\": \"44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-0bb88db782dbb846de19\"], \"delivery\": \"Originals queued for the next model request; large batches may span requests.\"}}, {\"tool\": \"read_pdf\", \"result\": {\"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-43852c44687baca48e12\", \"ev-4609a2662ec458fe5e71\", \"ev-c86a87a1f4e38c6715bf\"], \"delivery\": \"Originals queued for the next model request; large batches may span requests.\"}}]\nCurrent action failed; correct this error and continue:\nError in code parsing:\nExpecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0)\nMake sure to provide correct code blobs.\nEvidence ev-